INSERT INTO paper_sections (id,paper_id,position,kind,title,instructions,paragraphs_json,study_paragraphs_json) VALUES ('cet4-2023-12-1-section-5','cet4-2023-12-1',4,'reading','仔细阅读 · Passage Two（51–55）','There are 2 passages in this section. Each passage is followed by some questions or unfinished statements. For each of them there are four choices marked A),B),C)and D).You should decide on the best choice and mark the corresponding letter on Answer Sheet 2 with a single line through the centre.','["Female employees consistently pay lower airfares than men do for the same flights because they tend to book earlier.","We compared the airfare paid by employees in the same position within a company for the same class of travel and used a common statistical technique to account for other factors that might affect differences in airfares. We found that women paid on average $18 less per ticket than their male colleagues. Further investigation allowed us to conclude that this gap is largely explained by the fact that women tended to book earlier than men, 1.8 days on average.","We wanted to determine what was causing these gender differences in booking business trips so we tested a variety of possible explanations, such as women choosing to plan ahead or male frequent travelers being inclined to book late. None of these explained away the gender gap, so we applied data collected from surveys that express consumer preferences that play a central role in economic decisions, such as patience and risk avoidance.","We found that only the concept of \"negative reciprocity\"—in which an employee who feels unfairly treated engages in negative behaviors, such as spending their company''s money less carefully-explains these differences. The surveys showed men tend to exhibit more of these negative behaviors than women. This isn''t to say that all men engage in these behaviors—or that booking relatively late is a sign of abnormal behavior. It only means that the gender gap disappears when we plug in the negative reciprocity variable.","Prior research on negative reciprocity among workers found that it can result in lower employee motivation, business performance and workplace morale (士气) and culture.","Our results show another way these negative behaviors can manifest themselves, like in airline bookings, and add to evidence that women are less likely to engage in them.","Companies spend significant sums of money on business travel. While that $18 difference per ticket may seem small, it adds up. Our analysis suggests early booking by women can translate into savings of $1 million a year for a large multinational company with 20,000 regular travelers."]','["Female employees consistently pay lower airfares than men do for the same flights because they tend to book earlier.","We compared the airfare paid by employees in the same position within a company for the same class of travel and used a common statistical technique to account for other factors that might affect differences in airfares. We found that women paid on average $18 less per ticket than their male colleagues. Further investigation allowed us to conclude that this gap is largely explained by the fact that women tended to book earlier than men, 1.8 days on average.","We wanted to determine what was causing these gender differences in booking business trips so we tested a variety of possible explanations, such as women choosing to plan ahead or male frequent travelers being inclined to book late. None of these explained away the gender gap, so we applied data collected from surveys that express consumer preferences that play a central role in economic decisions, such as patience and risk avoidance.","We found that only the concept of \"negative reciprocity\"—in which an employee who feels unfairly treated engages in negative behaviors, such as spending their company''s money less carefully-explains these differences. The surveys showed men tend to exhibit more of these negative behaviors than women. This isn''t to say that all men engage in these behaviors—or that booking relatively late is a sign of abnormal behavior. It only means that the gender gap disappears when we plug in the negative reciprocity variable.","Prior research on negative reciprocity among workers found that it can result in lower employee motivation, business performance and workplace morale (士气) and culture.","Our results show another way these negative behaviors can manifest themselves, like in airline bookings, and add to evidence that women are less likely to engage in them.","Companies spend significant sums of money on business travel. While that $18 difference per ticket may seem small, it adds up. Our analysis suggests early booking by women can translate into savings of $1 million a year for a large multinational company with 20,000 regular travelers."]') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,kind=EXCLUDED.kind,title=EXCLUDED.title,instructions=EXCLUDED.instructions,paragraphs_json=EXCLUDED.paragraphs_json,study_paragraphs_json=EXCLUDED.study_paragraphs_json;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2023-12-1-section-5-q-51','cet4-2023-12-1-section-5',0,'choice','51. What did the author''s team conclude about the gender difference in airfares from their further investigation?','[{"key":"A","text":"It is largely attributed to women booking earlier than men."},{"key":"B","text":"It is largely explained by women''s choosing cheaper flights."},{"key":"C","text":"It is mainly accounted for by male employees'' readiness to pay more."},{"key":"D","text":"It is due to the fact that women care more about their company''s money."}]','A','参考答案 A，依据原文整理。第二段的进一步调查发现，女性平均比男性提前 1.8 天订票，主要解释了同等航班票价的性别差异。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2023-12-1-section-5-q-52','cet4-2023-12-1-section-5',1,'choice','52. What did the researchers want to determine by testing a variety of possible explanations?','[{"key":"A","text":"What made male frequent travelers book air tickets late."},{"key":"B","text":"What caused women to plan ahead in booking business trips."},{"key":"C","text":"What motivated women to book cheaper flights."},{"key":"D","text":"What accounted for the gender gap in airfares."}]','D','参考答案 D，依据原文整理。第三段明确说研究者要确定商务旅行订票的性别差异由什么导致，因此测试了多种可能解释。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2023-12-1-section-5-q-53','cet4-2023-12-1-section-5',2,'choice','53. What happened when the negative reciprocity variable was taken into account?','[{"key":"A","text":"Both men and women were found to engage in negative behaviors."},{"key":"B","text":"Neither men nor women viewed booking late as a bad behavior."},{"key":"C","text":"The gender difference in airfare expenses no longer existed."},{"key":"D","text":"The gender gap tended to narrow to a significant degree."}]','C','参考答案 C，依据原文整理。第四段末句说，加入负面互惠变量后，票价的性别差异消失。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2023-12-1-section-5-q-54','cet4-2023-12-1-section-5',3,'choice','54. What did prior research on negative reciprocity among workers find?','[{"key":"A","text":"It can do more harm to the workplace than to employees."},{"key":"B","text":"It contributes to the male-female divide in the workplace."},{"key":"C","text":"It proves to be counterproductive in a number of ways."},{"key":"D","text":"It can result in increasing labor-management conflicts."}]','C','参考答案 C，依据原文整理。此前研究指出负面互惠会降低员工积极性、企业绩效和工作场所士气及文化，说明它在多个方面起反作用。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
INSERT INTO questions (id,section_id,position,type,prompt,options_json,answer_text,explanation,points) VALUES ('cet4-2023-12-1-section-5-q-55','cet4-2023-12-1-section-5',4,'choice','55. What does the author emphasize about their analysis in the last paragraph?','[{"key":"A","text":"It can help companies increase their savings significantly."},{"key":"B","text":"It can duly contribute to companies’ business performance."},{"key":"C","text":"It can translate women''s booking practice into men''s behavior."},{"key":"D","text":"It can enhance large multinational companies'' competitiveness."}]','A','参考答案 A，依据原文整理。末段强调单张票节省 18 美元虽然看似不多，但累积后可为大型跨国公司一年节省约 100 万美元。',2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET position=EXCLUDED.position,type=EXCLUDED.type,prompt=EXCLUDED.prompt,options_json=EXCLUDED.options_json,answer_text=EXCLUDED.answer_text,explanation=EXCLUDED.explanation,points=EXCLUDED.points;
